WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Here's an answer that sounds right but on

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.920
its own explains nothing: Le Chatelier's principle says

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:06.960
it shifts right.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.280
By the end you'll know what to write

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:09.920
instead.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.200
We'll work through three types of equilibrium question

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.800
in full: explain with collision theory, graphs after

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.120
a change, and the no-shift traps.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.720
Then you try two.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.400
Temperature, industry and open systems come in part

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:24.960
two.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.566
Type one, the one that catches the most

00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:31.606
people: explain with collision theory.

00:00:31.927 --> 00:00:34.966
A rigid sealed container holds hydrogen and carbon

00:00:35.047 --> 00:00:38.726
dioxide, making water vapour and carbon monoxide, at

00:00:38.847 --> 00:00:39.526
equilibrium.

00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:42.006
A drying agent removes some of the water

00:00:42.087 --> 00:00:44.486
vapour, and the temperature does not change.

00:00:45.047 --> 00:00:47.686
Using collision theory, explain the effect on the

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.846
concentration of carbon monoxide.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.846
Underline the givens: rigid, so the volume is

00:00:53.927 --> 00:00:57.606
fixed; water removed; and the species to finish

00:00:57.687 --> 00:00:59.286
on, carbon monoxide.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.900
Build the answer in the order things happen.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.820
One, the change.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.580
Water vapour is removed, so its concentration falls.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.660
Two, collisions.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.260
Fewer water molecules means fewer collisions per second

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.460
between water and carbon monoxide, so the reverse

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.420
rate falls.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.700
The reaction is the whole change; the rate

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.220
is how fast it happens.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.460
Three, the other rate.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.180
The forward rate has not changed yet, so

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.300
it is now bigger.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.660
Four, the net result.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.740
More carbon monoxide is made than used, so

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.220
its concentration ends higher than at the first

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.020
equilibrium.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.860
Five, the level.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.660
The rates move together until they are equal

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:43.220
again.

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.313
Three classic slips.

00:01:46.594 --> 00:01:49.233
Writing only that Le Chatelier's principle says it

00:01:49.314 --> 00:01:50.353
shifts right.

00:01:50.594 --> 00:01:53.233
When the question asks for collision theory, or

00:01:53.314 --> 00:01:56.273
for why, that only repeats what happens.

00:01:56.754 --> 00:01:59.553
Use the principle to predict the direction, then

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:00.833
give the rate reason.

00:02:01.314 --> 00:02:04.273
Writing that the forward reaction increases, when you

00:02:04.354 --> 00:02:05.713
mean the forward rate.

00:02:06.114 --> 00:02:08.993
And stopping at shifts right without naming carbon

00:02:09.074 --> 00:02:09.793
monoxide.

00:02:10.194 --> 00:02:12.753
Finish on the species the question asked about.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:17.086
Type two: graphs after a disturbance.

00:02:17.727 --> 00:02:19.726
N O two and N two O four

00:02:19.967 --> 00:02:22.686
are at equilibrium in a one litre cylinder,

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.446
with the amounts given in the question.

00:02:25.087 --> 00:02:27.566
At time t one, the volume is halved

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.846
at constant temperature.

00:02:29.407 --> 00:02:32.686
Describe the graph of concentration against time, then

00:02:32.727 --> 00:02:35.406
the graph of amount in moles against time.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.353
Start with the squeeze.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:42.153
Concentration is amount divided by volume, so the

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:45.113
same particles in half the space double both

00:02:45.194 --> 00:02:48.793
concentrations at once, straight up, from 0.200 to

00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:53.833
0.400 and from 0.300 to

00:02:53.954 --> 00:02:56.713
0.600.

00:02:56.794 --> 00:02:59.713
That vertical jump is the squeeze, not the

00:02:59.754 --> 00:03:00.473
reaction.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:02.740
Now the response.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.420
Two gas particles become one, so the squeeze

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.100
favours the forward reaction.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.900
N O two curves down and N two

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.380
O four curves up, with N O two

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.180
changing by twice as much, because the equation

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.820
says two to one.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.980
Both level off together on ruled flat lines.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.540
N O two settles above where it started

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.860
and below where the squeeze sent it.

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.946
Now the amount in moles.

00:03:29.227 --> 00:03:32.186
The squeeze added and removed no particles, so

00:03:32.227 --> 00:03:34.026
there is no jump at all.

00:03:34.107 --> 00:03:36.666
N O two curves smoothly down and N

00:03:36.747 --> 00:03:39.306
two O four curves up, still two to

00:03:39.387 --> 00:03:39.786
one.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.600
So read the axis label first.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:44.920
Three slips.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.120
On this graph, a jump, or curves that

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.160
break the two to one ratio.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:53.080
Back on the concentration graph, levelling off at

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.480
the old value, or at the jump.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.580
Type three: the no-shift traps.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.780
Argon is added to a rigid, insulated container

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.660
holding brown N O two and colourless N

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.420
two O four at equilibrium.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.980
The argon is at the same temperature as

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.620
the mixture.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.340
What happens to the colour, and does the

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:14.740
temperature change?

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.500
Argon is an inert gas and takes no

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:18.060
part.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:22.546
The method is one question: does Q still

00:04:22.627 --> 00:04:23.426
equal K?

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.946
Argon bumps into things, but the forward reaction

00:04:27.027 --> 00:04:29.186
needs two N O two molecules to meet

00:04:29.587 --> 00:04:31.666
and the reverse needs N two O four

00:04:31.827 --> 00:04:34.386
to split, and the reacting gases are no

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:35.666
more crowded.

00:04:35.707 --> 00:04:38.466
The volume is fixed, so every concentration is

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:42.626
unchanged, both rates stay equal, and nothing happens.

00:04:42.707 --> 00:04:44.466
The colour is the same.

00:04:44.547 --> 00:04:47.026
With no net reaction, no heat is released

00:04:47.107 --> 00:04:50.146
or absorbed, so the temperature is the same.

00:04:50.227 --> 00:04:52.946
A catalyst and an added pure solid, which

00:04:53.027 --> 00:04:55.586
K leaves out, are in the same family.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.160
Two slips: pressure rises, so it shifts to

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.760
fewer particles, and pressure rises, so the temperature

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:04.720
rises.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.000
Pressure alone is not a disturbance here: no

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.640
net reaction, no net heat change.

00:05:11.867 --> 00:05:12.506
Your turn.

00:05:12.827 --> 00:05:16.266
Nitrogen and hydrogen make ammonia in a rigid

00:05:16.427 --> 00:05:18.746
sealed container, at equilibrium.

00:05:19.227 --> 00:05:22.186
Some extra nitrogen is injected, and the temperature

00:05:22.347 --> 00:05:23.386
does not change.

00:05:24.027 --> 00:05:26.826
Using collision theory, explain the effect on the

00:05:26.907 --> 00:05:28.426
concentration of hydrogen.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.346
For now, decide:

00:05:30.907 --> 00:05:34.186
which rate changes first, and does the hydrogen

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.426
concentration rise or fall?

00:05:36.987 --> 00:05:38.266
Pause here to answer.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.306
Then, in your own time, write the full

00:05:51.387 --> 00:05:53.866
five lines and check them against this.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:56.906
The species to finish on is hydrogen, not

00:05:56.987 --> 00:05:58.146
the one you added.

00:05:58.507 --> 00:06:01.626
More nitrogen means more collisions between nitrogen and

00:06:01.707 --> 00:06:05.066
hydrogen each second, so the forward rate rises

00:06:05.227 --> 00:06:07.786
while the reverse rate has not changed.

00:06:08.027 --> 00:06:10.826
Forward is now faster, so hydrogen is used

00:06:10.907 --> 00:06:13.466
up, and its concentration ends lower than at

00:06:13.547 --> 00:06:15.226
the first equilibrium.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.866
If you wrote that hydrogen increases, or that

00:06:17.947 --> 00:06:21.066
the forward reaction increases, check the species and

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:21.946
say rate.

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:24.766
One more, a graph.

00:06:24.847 --> 00:06:29.006
Nitrogen, hydrogen and ammonia are at equilibrium in

00:06:29.087 --> 00:06:31.806
a sealed cylinder at constant temperature.

00:06:31.887 --> 00:06:34.846
At time t one, something changes.

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:36.686
Both graphs are on screen.

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:39.806
Which disturbance was it: a substance added, the

00:06:39.887 --> 00:06:43.406
volume changed, the temperature changed, or a catalyst

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:44.286
added?

00:06:44.447 --> 00:06:45.566
Pause here to answer.

00:06:55.967 --> 00:06:58.726
The volume changed, and it was decreased.

00:06:59.007 --> 00:07:01.886
Every gas concentration jumped up together, so it

00:07:01.967 --> 00:07:04.206
was not one substance added.

00:07:04.447 --> 00:07:06.686
Temperature would show no jump on the concentration

00:07:06.847 --> 00:07:07.566
graph.

00:07:07.647 --> 00:07:09.886
A catalyst would change nothing.

00:07:09.927 --> 00:07:12.206
The amount graph has no jump, which fits

00:07:12.287 --> 00:07:15.166
volume as well as temperature, so the concentration

00:07:15.247 --> 00:07:16.366
graph decides.

00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:19.646
Find the words that give the type away.

00:07:20.127 --> 00:07:24.366
Using collision theory, explain: the five lines, ending

00:07:24.447 --> 00:07:26.126
on the named species.

00:07:26.447 --> 00:07:29.966
Sketch or describe a graph: axis label first,

00:07:30.047 --> 00:07:31.486
then what jumps.

00:07:31.727 --> 00:07:35.406
Argon, catalyst or added solid: does Q still

00:07:35.487 --> 00:07:36.406
equal K?

00:07:36.687 --> 00:07:39.006
Part two takes on the calculations.

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:41.673
Here are the key notes.

00:07:41.914 --> 00:07:43.833
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:43.914 --> 00:07:44.713
to copy them.
